        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="REI01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William Hamilton</forename>
                        <surname>Reid</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1784">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1827"/>
                    <occupation>poet</occupation>
                    <occupation>controversialist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>One of the more mercurial and shadowy figures of London radical
    circles who moves from radicalism to loyalism and back. The links in the diary make the identification plausible. He is associated with visits to 
      <persName key="MUI01">Muir</persName> and <persName key="PAL01">Palmer</persName> after their
    trials, then a series of links through <persName key="PHI01">Phillips</persName> and publishing circles; then a group associated
    with attendance at Hazlitt's lectures and with <persName key="HAZ01">Hazlitt</persName>. We cannot be certain that this is the
    Reid whom Godwin notes but it seems highly likely that Godwin would have made his acquaintance -
    possibly even before the Diary begins given Reid's association with the <title>Rolliad</title>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
